{
  "schema": "mva.community-allele-function-scorecard/v1",
  "privacy_class": "synthetic",
  "purpose": "Synthetic genotype scorecard. assessment_status is for a prespecified defect claim: positive means the defect claim was supported, negative means it was not, not_assessable means the assay was not valid for that row. assay_class wet is a filled lab handoff in this fixture, not a computational substitute. condition_class basal means the defect or reversal was present without imposed extrinsic stress; disease mitotic failure is not imposed extrinsic stress. system_class cellular means the defect or reversal was present in cells; a purified-protein thermal shift is not a cellular hypomorph and cannot satisfy genetic reversal. expression_class endogenous means the protein came from the edited locus; a transgene, cDNA, or overexpression row cannot mint a hypomorph or satisfy genetic reversal. specimen_class assay_matched means the assay used the confirmed genotype line; an unmatched line cannot mint a hypomorph. exact_corrected allele_specificity exact means the reversal used the exact allele; analog, homolog, or nearby cannot reverse an exact missense defect. recreated_missense allele_specificity exact means restoration used the exact allele; analog, homolog, nearby, or unlabeled cannot restore an exact missense defect.",
